+// (request, kv head, 24-token query block). Rank r attends to its half of the unit's key tiles; the halves meet at
+// the absolute scale 2^m through distributed shared memory (st.async) and each rank finishes 12 of the 24 tokens.
+// SLA_FUSED: the CTAs also do qkv_post2's work (QK-norm, RoPE, FP8 Q into shared memory, the new keys' cache rows
+// and packed tiles); new-key tiles are loaded once every producer of that head has published (ready counter).
+// flagjoin: the cached-key packing (sla_pack, side stream) is awaited through a done counter, not a graph edge.
+typedef unsigned int u32;
